1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,300
Every AI reply sounds the same.
Polite, tidy, nothing like you.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:07,800
My friends would spot it in a second.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:12,500
This is SaySo, a keyboard
that writes the way you'd say it.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:16,000
I type a plain draft,
tap the sparkle,

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,000
and get versions in my own voice.

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:24,500
And I don't send one long paragraph,
I send bursts.

7
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:29,000
So SaySo does too: a series,
stacked like notifications.

8
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:32,000
Tap, send. Next. Send.

9
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,800
Same meaning, my rhythm.

10
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:38,500
A friend asks for help on Saturday,
and I can't.

11
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,500
I double-tap the back of my phone.

12
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:45,000
SaySo grabs the screen
and asks who it's for.

13
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:48,000
I add a note:
politely decline.

14
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:54,500
Muse Spark reads the chat and writes
three replies the way I would.

15
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,800
Pick one, paste, send.

16
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,500
My voice comes from my own chats.

17
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:06,500
I drop in a WhatsApp export,
SaySo asks which one is me,

18
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:10,500
and tests itself on messages
it hasn't seen.

19
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:16,800
Sounds like me: 78%.
Generic AI: 41%.

20
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:19,500
Chats are how I text.

21
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:25,000
For emails and essays, I add things I wrote myself:
photos of old essays, a few sent emails.

22
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:30,800
SaySo takes my voice from them,
not their structure or content.

23
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:33,000
Now an essay.

24
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:37,500
I paste the question and just talk:
what I built, what broke, what I learned.

25
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:40,500
Muse Voice Transcribe writes it down.

26
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:45,500
SaySo plans it and writes it in my formal voice,
only from my own facts.

27
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:48,500
No "in today's fast-paced world".

28
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,000
Then it asks what would make it stronger.

29
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:55,500
I answer out loud, and it's revised.

30
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:59,800
Emails work the same way.

31
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,500
Too long? Thumbs down: "shorter."

32
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:06,500
It rewrites and remembers the rule.

33
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:10,500
Every message I send with SaySo's keys
becomes a new example right away,

34
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:13,800
and I can delete any of them.

35
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:16,500
Under the hood, four Meta models.

36
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:20,500
Muse Spark Open, open weights,
writes in my style.

37
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:23,500
Muse Spark 1.3 reads screenshots.

38
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,800
Muse Voice Transcribe listens.

39
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:32,800
And my own LoRA on Muse Glimmer 30B
is trained and benchmarked, waiting for a GPU.

40
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,500
Only my own writing is stored.

41
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:41,000
Other people's messages, screenshots and voice notes
are read in memory, then dropped.

42
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:44,500
SaySo.
Your words, your voice.

43
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,800
And you always press send.
